  "actor_notes": "Corvin.\nBEARING: Twenty-two, Sword of the Lake in white, honest open face, rows well. Stands very straight when nervous, which is most of the time.\nSPEECH: Too fast and too much. Volunteers help before checking whether he is allowed to. Apologises. Calls people \"sir\" and \"my lady\" indiscriminately and gets it wrong about a third of the time.\nTELL: He helps FIRST and thinks afterwards -- steps in, takes the weight, gives away the information -- and you can watch him realise, a beat late, what he has just done.\nWANTS: The white belt.\nWON'T: Lie. Leave somebody standing in trouble. Be quiet when he thinks something is wrong.\nBECAUSE: He is brave and not remotely subtle and he badly wants Temerach to notice, and he would rather be wrong and useful than right and late."
